<section class="phero"><div class="phero-media"><img src="/assets/img/photos/farm-field.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/farm-field-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/farm-field.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="900" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><a href="/towns-we-cover/">Towns we cover</a><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><span aria-current="page">Presque Isle</span></nav><p class="kicker">The County (Aroostook) · Aroostook County</p><h1>Insurance Appraiser in Presque Isle, Maine</h1><p class="lede">In Presque Isle, snow load, deep cold and farm buildings drive most claims. We review carrier estimates for homes, potato storage houses and businesses across Aroostook County, and serve as appraiser when needed.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-coral" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg><span>Call (844) 537-1427</span></a><a class="btn btn-line light" href="/reach-us/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="spec"><div><dt>County</dt><dd>Aroostook County</dd></div><div><dt>Region</dt><dd>The County (Aroostook)</dd></div><div><dt>Inspections</dt><dd>On site</dd></div></dl></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose"><div class="snap"><h2>Presque Isle at a glance</h2><dl>
<div><dt>County</dt><dd>Aroostook County</dd></div><div><dt>Region</dt><dd>The County (Aroostook)</dd></div>
<div class="wide"><dt>Neighborhoods and villages</dt><dd><ul class="chips"><li>Downtown Main Street</li><li>UMPI campus area</li><li>Chapman</li><li>Mapleton</li><li>Easton</li><li>Westfield</li></ul></dd></div>
<div class="wide"><dt>Housing mix</dt><dd>Capes, ranches and two-story farmhouses in town, older wood-frame homes near downtown, and potato storage houses, pole barns and metal farm buildings across the surrounding farmland.</dd></div>
<div class="wide"><dt>Common claim risks</dt><dd><ul class="chips coral"><li>Snow load collapse</li><li>Ice dams</li><li>Frozen pipes</li><li>Farm building wind</li></ul></dd></div></dl>
<h3>Storms on record</h3><ol class="mini-storms"><li><b>Mar 2008</b><span><strong>Record snow winter.</strong> Heavy snow and rain loaded roofs; buildings collapsed in Presque Isle and nearby County towns.</span></li><li><b>Apr 2008</b><span><strong>Spring flood.</strong> Snowmelt and rain flooded northern Maine rivers; the worst damage came at Fort Kent.</span></li><li><b>Dec 1973</b><span><strong>Aroostook River flood.</strong> Rare winter flood on the Aroostook damaged homes and camps along the river near Presque Isle.</span></li></ol></div>
<h2>Snow load is the headline</h2>
<p>Presque Isle gets some of the heaviest snow in New England, and the winter of 2007 to 2008 showed what that means for buildings. Nearby Caribou set a seasonal snowfall record, and in March 2008 heavy snow followed by rain loaded roofs across Aroostook County. Buildings collapsed in Presque Isle and other County towns, and city crews shoveled public roofs to head off more damage. An insurance appraiser in Presque Isle sees snow load claims nearly every winter, and the big years produce disputes over whether the damage was collapse, wear or poor maintenance.</p>
<p>Policies treat collapse in specific ways, and the definitions matter. The policy decides coverage; the estimate still has to capture shoring, framing and the cost of working in deep snow. Our <a href="/appraisal-work/ice-dam-snow-load-appraisal/">ice dam and snow load appraisal</a> page explains our approach.</p>
<h2>Farm buildings and The County economy</h2>
<p>Potato storage houses, pole barns and metal machine sheds dot the land around Presque Isle, Mapleton, Easton and Westfield. Their repair costs bear little resemblance to a house. Storage buildings may carry specialized insulation, ventilation and climate control, and a roof or wall failure can also put stored crops at risk if the policy covers them. Carrier software often prices these structures as generic outbuildings.</p>
<ul>
<li>Metal roofing and wall panels that must match existing profiles.</li>
<li>Insulation and ventilation systems in storage houses.</li>
<li>Engineering and permitting for structural repairs.</li>
<li>Equipment rental and access across snowbound farm lanes.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Homes in deep cold</h2>
<p>Presque Isle homes are mostly capes, ranches and farmhouses, many heated with oil or wood. Frozen pipes, ice dams and chimney fires are the common losses. A furnace failure at minus 20 can freeze a house in hours. Wood stove and chimney fires bring smoke damage that spreads further than it first appears.</p>
<h2>Rivers and spring melt</h2>
<p>Spring melt is its own season in The County. The April and May 2008 flood swamped northern Maine rivers, with the worst damage at Fort Kent, and the Aroostook River has flooded homes and camps near Presque Isle before, including in December 1973. River flooding is excluded under homeowners policies and requires separate flood coverage.</p>
<h2>Distance and timing</h2>
<p>Commercial buildings along Main Street and the businesses that serve the farm economy face the same snow and cold. Flat and low-slope roofs collect drifts, and rooftop equipment adds weight. When a roof sags or leaks, the estimate needs to account for snow removal, interior damage, inventory and the cost of working in winter.</p>
<p>Contractors are scarce and the building season is short this far north. Estimates that ignore travel, winter conditions and the wait for trades often come up short. A Presque Isle insurance appraiser should account for those realities. Start with our <a href="/claim-math/appraisal-file-strength-test/">appraisal file strength test</a> to see how ready your claim is. For coverage questions or deadlines, consult a Maine attorney.</p>

<h2>Appraisal work for Presque Isle properties</h2>
<p>Every Maine Insurance Appraiser service is available in Presque Isle and the surrounding towns, including:</p>
<ul><li><a href="/appraisal-work/homeowner-dispute-appraisal/">Homeowner Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-work/noreaster-hurricane-appraisal/">Nor’easter &amp; Hurricane Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-work/water-damage-loss-appraisal/">Water Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-work/ice-dam-snow-load-appraisal/">Ice Dam &amp; Snow Load Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-work/fallen-tree-limb-appraisal/">Fallen Tree Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-work/carrier-estimate-line-review/">Insurance Estimate Review</a></li></ul>
<h2>Presque Isle questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>My potato storage roof collapsed under snow. Will appraisal cover the building and the crop?</summary><p>Appraisal sets the amount of covered loss only. Whether the building and stored crops are covered depends on your farm or commercial policy, so read the collapse and property sections first.</p></details><details><summary>Why would a carrier say snow load damage is wear and tear?</summary><p>Carriers sometimes argue a roof failed from age or poor maintenance rather than the weight of snow. Photos, snow depth records and contractor findings help show what actually happened.</p></details><details><summary>Can appraisal include travel costs for contractors coming to Presque Isle?</summary><p>Yes, when those costs are a real part of the repair. Travel and lodging for trades are common in The County and belong in a fair estimate.</p></details></div>
